# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitLab does
# not render a "Cite this repository" panel the way GitHub does, but the format
# is forge-independent: cffconvert, Zenodo and the R package cffr all read it,
# which is why it still ships. Kept out of the CRAN tarball via .Rbuildignore.
# Once the package has a Zenodo DOI, add `doi:` and an `identifiers:` block.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ssrfr: Server-Side Request Forgery Guard for Outbound Requests"
abstract: >-
  Protects R applications that fetch URLs an attacker can influence from
  server-side request forgery. Each redirect hop is parsed once, resolved once,
  and every resolved address is classified before the connection is pinned to
  a validated address, so a hostname cannot be rebound between check and
  connect. Refusals carry stable reason codes.
version: 0.0.0.9000
authors:
  - family-names: Turczynski
    given-names: Bart
    email: bartek@turczynski.pl
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8788-7980"
repository-code: "https://gitlab.com/bart-turczynski/ssrfr"
url: "https://bart-turczynski.gitlab.io/ssrfr/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - R
  - rstats
  - security
  - SSRF
  - server-side request forgery
  - URL fetching
